silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_06_cheese_trap_typed_vs_unrestricted_sections_01_typed_vs_unrestricted_distinction_concrete_anchor_1_typed_english#typedenglish silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedEnglish is the gated fragment admitted by (tau_N, tau_V, R_O). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'typed_english', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
